<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Shipcracker armor's jump, granted through VEF's CompAbilitiesApparel on
    SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker and fuelled by the CompApparelReloadable on the same def.
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_PowerJump (1.6/Defs/AbilityDefs/Abilities.xml); the rules that
    differ live in ShipcrackerWarcasket.Ability_BreachJump (planet: ranged, no sight test;
    space: unlimited range, sight required; landing-only breach blast) and the numbers in the
    BreachJumpExtension below.

    fuelPerJump 20 of a 100-charge chemfuel tank (Aerial's numbers; 5 jumps per tank).
    breachDamage 20 is the pawn-facing number, split into 2 to 4 wounds by the SCWC_Breach def;
    Aerial's jump does 15, a frag grenade 50. Wall and building damage come from that def's
    factors (600 to a wall cell, 150 to a door or turret) and the shoulders' SCWC_BreachPower,
    which its worker applies to buildings only. breachArmorPenetration 0.15 (Aerial's works out
    at 0.225, a grenade's 0.75) is passed explicitly because GenExplosion otherwise derives
    penetration as damage x 0.015. breachRadius 2 gives a 13-cell footprint, small enough that a
    landing punches a door-sized hole through the wall it lands beside rather than levelling a
    room; vanilla's explosion still damages wall cells adjacent to the open cells it reaches.
    Wearer excluded; allies in the footprint are not, as with Aerial. requireLineOfSight is
    ignored by the ability class and set false only to document the planet rule. The blast
    radius is previewed at the hovered cell while targeting, and on a space map the reachable
    cells in view are outlined (see the ability class).

    roofPunchRadius 1 is one below breachRadius so the hole in the ceiling is tighter than the
    hole in the wall; the roof rules themselves live in the ability class. In space this vents
    the gravship room the wearer leaves or breaches into, which is the point of the set.

    Space flight runs at spaceFlightSpeedFactor 3 times the wearer's VFEP_FlightSpeed (36
    cells/s at the base 12; Aerial's full set reaches 27 on a planet), capped at
    spaceFlightMaxSeconds 4 so a hop past 144 cells speeds up rather than drags. The landing
    shockwave ring is the SCWC_Breach DamageDef's centre effecter; the launch cell gets none.

    "breach jump" is the planet label, "breach burn" the space one (vacuumLabel, applied to
    the gizmo and tooltip title by the ability class): space is a different enough experience
    to advertise under its own name, and "breach" in both ties them to the one tank and
    landing. The description carries no numbers (VEF appends range, radius and cast time; the
    range line drops out in space because SpaceRange is above its display cap) and no fuel line
    (the tank takes astrofuel at half the charges under VGE1). vacuumDescription is appended to
    the tooltip only when a loaded def can produce a space map, so players without Odyssey
    never read about a mode they cannot reach; an extension field rather than a patched
    description, because a patch from the gated root would drag the DefInjected entry for the
    same field into that root and collide with the main-tree entry whenever the gate is open.

    Icons are placeholders borrowed from VFEP until the commissioned art lands: Aerial's Power
    Jump on a planet, Shock's Blast Off (spaceIconPath) in space.

    flightEffecter / spaceFlightEffecter name the effecter the flyer plays for the whole flight,
    so a compat root can recolour it by patch. The main tree burns chemfuel and uses our orange
    copies of VFEP's exhausts (EffecterDefs/): Aerial's Power Jump effect on a planet, whose
    flame cuts out early to suit a short hop, and Shock's Blast Off in space, whose flame burns
    to the landing; both moved up to the mid-back thruster outlets. The Vanilla Gravship
    Expanded root switches the tank to astrofuel and these two to the purple astroflame pair
    defined there.

    thrusterGlowCurve maps cast progress (0 at the click, 1 as the flyer launches) to the
    opacity of the armor's thruster-outlet overlay (the render node declared in
    ThingDefs_Misc/Warcasket_Shipcracker.xml). Heat builds slowly and then rushes: a quarter
    opacity at 60% of the cast, most of it in the last third. The flight holds full opacity and
    there is no fade-out after landing or an interrupted cast; the ability class explains the
    state tracking.
  -->
  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
    <defName>SCWC_BreachJump</defName>
    <label>breach jump</label>
    <description>Use the armor's drop thrusters to jump to a location, landing hard enough to breach walls and hull plating. The jump is short but needs no clear path.</description>
    <abilityClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.Ability_BreachJump</abilityClass>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <iconPath>UI/Abilities/PowerJump</iconPath>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <keepCarryingThing>true</keepCarryingThing>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="ShipcrackerWarcasket.BreachJumpExtension">
        <fuelPerJump>20</fuelPerJump>
        <breachDamage>20</breachDamage>
        <breachArmorPenetration>0.15</breachArmorPenetration>
        <breachRadius>2</breachRadius>
        <roofPunchRadius>1</roofPunchRadius>
        <spaceFlightSpeedFactor>3</spaceFlightSpeedFactor>
        <spaceFlightMaxSeconds>4</spaceFlightMaxSeconds>
        <flightEffecter>SCWC_BreachJumpFlame</flightEffecter>
        <spaceFlightEffecter>SCWC_BreachBurnFlame</spaceFlightEffecter>
        <thrusterGlowCurve>
          <points>
            <li>(0, 0)</li>
            <li>(0.6, 0.25)</li>
            <li>(0.85, 0.65)</li>
            <li>(1, 1)</li>
          </points>
        </thrusterGlowCurve>
        <spaceIconPath>UI/Abilities/BlastOff</spaceIconPath>
        <vacuumDescription>In vacuum it has no range limit, but the way must be open.</vacuumDescription>
        <vacuumLabel>breach burn</vacuumLabel>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
</Defs>
